      "content": "Access Tuple Items"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Similar to lists, we use indexes to access tuple items."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "We use indexes to access tuple items",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's take an example."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1languages = ('Python', 'JavaScript', 'C++')\n2\n3# access first item\n4first_language = languages[0]\n5print(first_language)   # Python\n6\n7# access second item\n8print(languages[1])   # JavaScript\n9\n10# access third-last item\n11print(languages[-3])   # Python"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Similar to lists, if we try to access items using index that doesn't exist, we will get an error"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1languages = ('Python', 'JavaScript', 'C++')\n2\n3# try to access the fourth item using index 3\n4print(languages[3])"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "IndexError: tuple index out of range"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Our languages tuple has only 3 elements. If we try to access the fourth element using index 3, we will get an error."
    },
